      "requirement": "For compiled regex patterns containing a manual callout, the target's compile-context surface must reach the supported PCRE2_EXTRA_NEVER_CALLOUT state and observe rejection with PCRE2_ERROR_CALLOUT_CALLER_DISABLED.",
      "target_route": "Eight option bytes followed by a pattern such as a(?C)b enter LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput; it creates a compile context, sets only the compiled-length limit, and calls pcre2_compile with that context. The parser reads extra_options from the context and rejects (?C) only when the new bit is set.",
      "failure_condition": "No fuzzer input can set that context bit: the option word is masked into ordinary compile and match options, and the complete entry never sets compile extra options. Thus supported callout rejection remains unreachable.",
      "alternative_paths": "The second compile only resets ordinary compile options; matching and JIT occur after successful compilation. The parser's inline option handling does not set PCRE2_EXTRA_NEVER_CALLOUT, and normal callout handling does not produce the disabled-callout error.",
      "discovery_necessary": true,
      "discovery_established": true
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "candidate_id": "c1",
      "decision": "keep",
